+// Round 12 rework -- what the round 11 mechanism still got wrong,
+// proven on device in v13 and reproduced on the host harness. The
+// bar DID render in v13 (visible at the manager's top-right in the
+// device screenshots), but it never moved onto the modal error
+// dialog: it stayed on the manager, BEHIND the dialog's own
+// window, with the dialog covering its Minimize half. Root cause:
+// windowOf() resolved an event object to a window by walking the
+// QObject parent chain to the OUTERMOST widget ancestor. wxQt
+// creates every dialog's Qt widget parented to its owner frame's
+// widget, so for any parented dialog the walk overshoots the
+// dialog and lands on the owner frame -- the controller's notion
+// of "the current window" was pinned to the manager for every
+// KiCad dialog (the wizard included), and Close/Minimize would
+// have acted on the manager even with an editor in front.
+// windowOf() now uses QWidget::window(), which honours the
+// window flags and returns the dialog itself. Three supporting
+// changes: pickHost() prefers QApplication::activeModalWidget()
+// while a modal dialog is up, so manager-side events during a
+// modal session cannot pull the bar back; the bar is sized with
+// adjustSize() after re-parenting and re-anchored on the host's
+// Move events as well as Resize, with a fully opaque background
+// and a 44 pt hit height so it cannot be missed; and drags now
+// move the window through wxWindowQt::Move() -- the
+// wxWindowQt::DoMoveWindow() path whose iOS clamp (patch 0009)
+// this code previously bypassed with a raw QWidget::move() plus
+// a hand-copied clamp, desyncing wx's geometry bookkeeping from
+// the widget's real position.
+//
 // The implementation compiles only for iOS (Q_OS_IOS); other wxQt
 // builds get the empty stub at the bottom.
 // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
